n rights"}, {"id": "080a4be7-61e3-4018-b5fb-9d669971d814", "type": "concept", "title": "Escalation paths"}, {"id": "de694a58-ec64-41d3-9450-c42351521599", "type": "concept", "title": "Incentives"}], "description": "Gist: Good pricing needs marketing, sales, finance, product, operations, legal, and analytics to align."}]}, {"id": "41740646-be52-43d3-b583-9598793010d5", "type": "topic", "title": "Demand, Elasticity, and Market Response", "description": "Build the economic foundation for predicting how price changes affect volume, revenue, margin, and customer behavior.", "children": [{"id": "d443874c-582d-4d9e-94e8-5151c1e6eb88", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Demand curves", "children": [{"id": "4dc128a0-dacf-48fa-9f60-8ca3712abc3e", "type": "concept", "title": "Demand schedule"}, {"id": "48a4a539-8e94-4d1b-8ecb-37c6cf3ab393", "type": "concept", "title": "Market demand"}, {"id": "fcbfc9b7-34b2-444e-86bf-3c927d7241be", "type": "concept", "title": "Individual demand"}, {"id": "b4457692-c1eb-4c62-9c34-4542150355be", "type": "concept", "title": "Revenue curve"}], "description": "Gist: Students learn to reason from price to quantity and from quantity to revenue."}, {"id": "e2a8d32f-70af-42f0-9064-cb4f6b58a767", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Elasticity", "children": [{"id": "e11656c0-2b0d-4054-a29b-7602e203e0c6", "type": "concept", "title": "Own-price elasticity"}, {"id": "b3c6902b-1435-4d8b-909e-66191042ed7f", "type": "concept", "title": "Cross-price elasticity"}, {"id": "0505b20d-4edd-4970-8a40-b9e25f3a1210", "type": "concept", "title": "Income elasticity"}, {"id": "5e0542ec-0989-438d-a1b7-0c68329e1b43", "type": "concept", "title": "Arc elasticity"}], "description": "Gist: Elasticity tells managers how sensitive demand is to price changes."}, {"id": "4b103a97-ad85-4664-97c6-9a416125a4bd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Market response limits", "children": [{"id": "5aa44897-dbd1-47bf-8eb2-e41458e1a4f5", "type": "concept", "title": "Short-run versus long-run"}, {"id": "634536d8-6c2e-480e-bea2-71d885600c6f", "type": "concept", "title": "Stockpiling"}, {"id": "10a71674-55c0-449a-b054-28739269df64", "type": "concept", "title": "Reference prices"}, {"id": "2cf56157-d76f-49c4-be80-867bd21e57ea", "type": "concept", "title": "Competitive response"}], "description": "Gist: Elasticity estimates are useful but can shift with context, competition, and time."}]}, {"id": "3f0093af-6e7f-4c4a-937a-4af0e4553a1f", "type": "topic", "title": "Costs, Margins, and Contribution Economics", "description": "Connect pricing decisions to cost structure, contribution margin, break-even logic, and profitability.", "children": [{"id": "9de504f0-5c58-4676-ba45-4e7a3966fdb4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cost structures", "children": [{"id": "9c7ef365-9610-4543-a617-db0fb142775d", "type": "concept", "title": "Fixed costs"}, {"id": "f5ee87ab-f4d1-4df9-b033-83d40fba229d", "type": "concept", "title": "Variable costs"}, {"id": "6a5d543a-fdc6-4f29-8aca-be87aaf79815", "type": "concept", "title": "Marginal costs"}, {"id": "747c623b-bd35-4200-85a8-1cc0281f87f6", "type": "concept", "title": "Sunk costs"}], "description": "Gist: Pricing must account for fixed, variable, marginal, and capacity-driven costs."}, {"id": "9b84d3fc-f8a8-4118-bc80-78188884c258", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Contribution margin", "children": [{"id": "2dea8b66-9fe9-475c-a8ac-ff3c4b2e2162", "type": "concept", "title": "Unit contribution"}, {"id": "ef384c14-b28d-45c6-a814-8eecea40c8ec", "type": "concept", "title": "Gross margin"}, {"id": "ac26d1a0-835f-4782-a29b-d41025d01849", "type": "concept", "title": "Break-even volume"}, {"id": "6a797568-ccc6-4587-9a40-8a63c8f2122f", "type": "concept", "title": "Incremental profit"}], "description": "Gist: Contribution logic shows how price changes affect profit through both margin and volume."}, {"id": "e143c386-c64a-4e24-b68e-d5631578403c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cost traps", "children": [{"id": "83f60457-97e1-46fb-b85d-ad0f04c1ea09", "type": "concept", "title": "Cost allocation errors"}, {"id": "07266733-e37f-44e5-a743-407908ba3e20", "type": "concept", "title": "Volume assumptions"}, {"id": "be395154-5b92-4c2f-a08f-09eeaf7ae9ae", "type": "concept", "title": "Overhead burden"}, {"id": "b2b9fd93-bbe7-4464-a2a5-e76969aa1663", "type": "concept", "title": "Commodity thinking"}], "description": "Gist: Students learn why cost-plus pricing can be simple but strategically dangerous."}]}, {"id": "0e722f78-73b3-43d5-9b3b-a9da7ae8aa98", "type": "topic", "title": "Customer Value, Willingness to Pay, and Value-Based Pricing", "description": "Teach students to estimate and communicate value rather than defaulting to cost-plus or competitor-following prices.", "children": [{"id": "b169260b-128f-4d77-8631-b292955edc49", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Economic value to customer", "children": [{"id": "0e44a251-553d-46b4-90cf-10efeb97cff4", "type": "concept", "title": "Reference value"}, {"id": "93a55193-0e59-47fd-83a6-839eeaa0ccdf", "type": "concept", "title": "Differentiation value"}, {"id": "a9f1d585-e823-4fb3-9b7f-038684b8c7d2", "type": "concept", "title": "Total cost of ownership"}, {"id": "4932fee3-35e0-4de2-ad22-9acd3c9c9d2a", "type": "concept", "title": "ROI for customer"}], "description": "Gist: Value-based pricing starts by estimating what a solution is worth to the buyer."}, {"id": "8eea0405-de8c-4ec4-aa5b-958e87756ddd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Willingness to pay", "children": [{"id": "8b27fdb8-ba5c-46de-908e-47f4674e4cdc", "type": "concept", "title": "Conjoint basics"}, {"id": "84ee4b86-e1e1-40bc-9b0c-6aba96097e64", "type": "concept", "title": "Van Westendorp"}, {"id": "55b10d06-752c-4ce1-824d-d2513cd71538", "type": "concept", "title": "Gabor-Granger"}, {"id": "2559835b-86c8-470d-93f0-bd040c8dc4d5", "type": "concept", "title": "Revealed preference"}], "description": "Gist: Students learn practical ways to infer the price customers may accept."}, {"id": "c6e63d5b-7454-4ca7-a296-a2c535530b43", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Value communication", "children": [{"id": "f6cab7bb-03ef-4687-a14a-35ccca911a48", "type": "concept", "title": "Value proposition"}, {"id": "e3b3483f-9194-495e-b50e-2e7fb1388de7", "type": "concept", "title": "Proof points"}, {"id": "f04571e1-5e6d-4635-ab48-7e7b598d850f", "type": "concept", "title": "ROI calculator"}, {"id": "ae0c6fb0-7487-4ce0-9176-0b394b32490c", "type": "concept", "title": "Sales narrative"}], "description": "Gist: A price only works when the customer understands the value logic."}]}, {"id": "f355022a-25dd-4703-8ac7-1f5314d9fa6d", "type": "topic", "title": "Segmentation, Price Fences, and Differential Pricing", "description": "Show how different customers, occasions, and channels can support different prices without destroying trust.", "children": [{"id": "53b29d49-2891-499b-8084-3994580a81dd", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Segment logic", "children": [{"id": "cb6d3ad3-2c10-463f-b53f-79f2812be1a8", "type": "concept", "title": "Needs segments"}, {"id": "4507380f-8dc6-4133-bbda-98fd1d4a3431", "type": "concept", "title": "Usage segments"}, {"id": "84a98991-ba26-4a8f-addb-676b28f8167b", "type": "concept", "title": "Value segments"}, {"id": "23213b76-a5ad-4ff3-9751-e69e513b0e2c", "type": "concept", "title": "Channel segments"}], "description": "Gist: Different customer groups often have different needs, willingness to pay, and cost-to-serve."}, {"id": "67e34122-03c6-421c-99e7-feaa1215a745", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Price fences", "children": [{"id": "b908b85c-cccb-48d2-b856-d4a1e642aedc", "type": "concept", "title": "Student pricing"}, {"id": "f69d52d0-9a58-4dac-a91a-2920ad57bfaf", "type": "concept", "title": "Advance purchase"}, {"id": "38ae9bb8-a635-4d99-91aa-6723b3f2a158", "type": "concept", "title": "Volume tiers"}, {"id": "609601a2-0ba3-4bc9-9c4f-5dd577f92e12", "type": "concept", "title": "Time-based fences"}], "description": "Gist: Price fences let firms separate prices by conditions customers perceive as legitimate."}, {"id": "436afe69-669e-491d-b38c-e32cf5b4161b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Trust and leakage", "children": [{"id": "3c44c30f-96a3-4bbc-9017-88bacbe5d7cd", "type": "concept", "title": "Arbitrage"}, {"id": "efcf4742-c4c4-459e-866c-17c9ffeccbc5", "type": "concept", "title": "Grey markets"}, {"id": "8ba26c37-fc10-4782-9f31-5b0ec984cf64", "type": "concept", "title": "Fairness perceptions"}, {"id": "bfb831ab-f0ad-4649-970c-3fdfce2c4623", "type": "concept", "title": "Fence enforcement"}], "description": "Gist: Differential pricing must manage arbitrage, resentment, and channel conflict."}]}, {"id": "d6c7e89c-8320-465b-a5c5-4ee45256cace", "type": "topic", "title": "Competitive Pricing, Game Theory, and Strategic Interaction", "description": "Analyze price competition, retaliation, signaling, price wars, and strategic response in real markets.", "children": [{"id": "b1e1981e-570a-4c44-90d2-a2f0386cb035", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Competitive landscape", "children": [{"id": "efb2a946-894d-49d8-90dd-d5d159e92ff4", "type": "concept", "title": "Direct rivals"}, {"id": "ecd340fe-cf4e-4fe9-bb75-1a3cf0122818", "type": "concept", "title": "Substitutes"}, {"id": "e4b48335-95b1-4b25-8847-7b2d8f9beaf5", "type": "concept", "title": "Market concentration"}, {"id": "5803383f-6864-4080-9a85-67991bb05e98", "type": "concept", "title": "Switching costs"}], "description": "Gist: Students evaluate how price moves depend on substitutes, rivals, entry, and market power."}, {"id": "481a5ec8-8316-419a-9947-c7809866bab1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Strategic interaction", "children": [{"id": "0e079b65-582b-4554-bd92-3b09237ae7fb", "type": "concept", "title": "Price war"}, {"id": "284da315-49ab-433a-a691-4c4997defae8", "type": "concept", "title": "Best response"}, {"id": "0211a616-9fcd-4bd9-9a9d-cb4a6d7d5e1b", "type": "concept", "title": "Repeated games"}, {"id": "e415bd77-6b18-4d7e-81f3-6aecfbddac5f", "type": "concept", "title": "Credible commitments"}], "description": "Gist: Pricing decisions can trigger retaliation, accommodation, signaling, or collusion risk."}, {"id": "24e1c2dc-8360-42a5-9e31-1dac14f03d07", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Competitive intelligence", "children": [{"id": "41ead15d-f1db-441d-b585-a92449d04fc8", "type": "concept", "title": "Price tracking"}, {"id": "2075c851-aa9c-4f5a-b299-d83e0eacff20", "type": "concept", "title": "Feature comparison"}, {"id": "b3a3a962-66db-4101-82d7-86ef870dac2d", "type": "concept", "title": "Value equivalence"}, {"id": "9e8344e2-6d36-426d-88d0-63f9ceca21bb", "type": "concept", "title": "Response thresholds"}], "description": "Gist: Students learn to interpret competitor prices without blindly matching them."}]}, {"id": "c6f58803-6603-48d0-aac5-0abbad521f11", "type": "topic", "title": "Price Discrimination, Bundling, and Versioning", "description": "Study advanced price architecture for capturing heterogeneous willingness to pay.", "children": [{"id": "bb22ce2e-4cac-4791-a423-63fdd4e999e7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Price discrimination", "children": [{"id": "8eb0a751-a350-4056-a423-e042607b10b2", "type": "concept", "title": "First-degree intuition"}, {"id": "01cb184e-05cc-4ab4-8abe-25fc21ceaa44", "type": "concept", "title": "Second-degree menus"}, {"id": "480a9cb2-9b0b-4066-a516-4373eb7d2323", "type": "concept", "title": "Third-degree segments"}, {"id": "ea182cca-1871-40f3-9ee6-1d6023b7cb20", "type": "concept", "title": "Two-part tariffs"}], "description": "Gist: Firms capture more value when they can serve customers with different willingness to pay."}, {"id": "47734b9b-fbc1-4467-a2eb-65afe161af74", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Bundling", "children": [{"id": "fa15de1f-c771-4b09-9056-91d349a3c99d", "type": "concept", "title": "Pure bundling"}, {"id": "45157cec-944c-4f3a-8f64-d924bbcc5a67", "type": "concept", "title": "Mixed bundling"}, {"id": "d33d031d-b0c5-4a8d-b412-bcd18cfad919", "type": "concept", "title": "Tying"}, {"id": "1bea06e0-d93b-45ee-bea1-de59657590a2", "type": "concept", "title": "Unbundling"}], "description": "Gist: Bundling can increase value capture, simplify choice, or hide component prices."}, {"id": "5a773cc8-c1fa-4219-9013-6ebcb1f5887b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Versioning", "children": [{"id": "2eb65969-499e-4799-be5b-7d8aad27c8b3", "type": "concept", "title": "Feature fences"}, {"id": "4de7b397-f6b0-4e3a-a6e3-bcadfe20c203", "type": "concept", "title": "Quality tiers"}, {"id": "74edc9cc-bf30-4d0c-90f6-26d3243a82d7", "type": "concept", "title": "Add-ons"}, {"id": "af60ab78-1d39-4ad0-8eef-52999aa9930f", "type": "concept", "title": "Upgrade paths"}], "description": "Gist: Good-better-best architecture gives customers choices while steering value capture."}]}, {"id": "6189bde0-d7bb-41cf-bb6e-080e914c344c", "type": "topic", "title": "Behavioral Pricing and Price Psychology", "description": "Use behavioral economics to understand framing, anchors, fairness, reference prices, and perceived value.", "children": [{"id": "d755b26e-c772-49a3-86ba-d695d3bd6102", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Reference prices", "children": [{"id": "4fff2caf-6e03-4709-8f10-e80192fcae57", "type": "concept", "title": "Internal reference price"}, {"id": "cddc06a1-2843-4b6b-9223-0ca7a29650bc", "type": "concept", "title": "External reference price"}, {"id": "26cdc223-8024-49d6-ba5d-b38715cd5268", "type": "concept", "title": "Anchoring"}, {"id": "2bac82b3-6873-460a-a192-ec19e321e7a0", "type": "concept", "title": "Decoy effects"}], "description": "Gist: Consumers judge prices relative to anchors, memory, and comparison sets."}, {"id": "a4efb54a-d838-48dc-9540-36ed9a116e4d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Framing and presentation", "children": [{"id": "af7bb8e9-5227-4b4d-8681-ffea7d61058b", "type": "concept", "title": "Charm pricing"}, {"id": "4b0f45c6-ad05-4508-a5b0-a4448a91c5ff", "type": "concept", "title": "Partitioned pricing"}, {"id": "9bc5a60f-33bd-47fc-a11b-34d39a0be8fa", "type": "concept", "title": "Monthly framing"}, {"id": "24f32105-ac99-4197-a6ee-784d03ecdd26", "type": "concept", "title": "Discount framing"}], "description": "Gist: How price is presented can change perceived pain, fairness, and value."}, {"id": "f78f2562-4fa1-4b8f-9d3c-15268d1de5f3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Fairness and trust", "children": [{"id": "af875376-8d43-41c2-8932-4be3e9e10c8d", "type": "concept", "title": "Price fairness"}, {"id": "1ef6fa5b-cd14-403d-906b-fa1a56ede910", "type": "concept", "title": "Surge pricing backlash"}, {"id": "cd66af43-dc61-4a47-9ba4-6077d63a748e", "type": "concept", "title": "Hidden fees"}, {"id": "d2d3a003-ada7-4b55-87de-daf3b98b4264", "type": "concept", "title": "Transparency"}], "description": "Gist: Pricing can damage trust when customers perceive exploitation or opacity."}]}, {"id": "73eb79d6-3f87-4305-8c8e-fb9fae5b4a2c", "type": "topic", "title": "Product Line, Portfolio, and Lifecycle Pricing", "description": "Coordinate prices across products, upgrades, complements, launches, maturity, and end-of-life decisions.", "children": [{"id": "a27b246f-c26e-4607-9243-6b1e78a0f63b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Line architecture", "children": [{"id": "1b764f96-4b20-44d6-a062-61e9c7209407", "type": "concept", "title": "Entry product"}, {"id": "b3153387-cccc-4abf-98a2-22890e5d58f1", "type": "concept", "title": "Core product"}, {"id": "d8cc2eea-747f-45b9-87c3-dbd744e664cc", "type": "concept", "title": "Premium tier"}, {"id": "d4654dd7-14a3-4ab2-b7a3-73cbad9ad741", "type": "concept", "title": "Feature ladder"}], "description": "Gist: Products in a line should be priced to clarify choice and protect margin."}, {"id": "75c3ebef-6992-474a-afff-d70e67683a2e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Lifecycle pricing", "children": [{"id": "45a7f669-9023-4ca3-9206-9eae695b7d62", "type": "concept", "title": "Skimming"}, {"id": "981b1cdc-86f1-4eaa-90e2-bd269d507350", "type": "concept", "title": "Penetration pricing"}, {"id": "01c080e8-d302-489c-893a-8642b135c9ce", "type": "concept", "title": "Harvesting"}, {"id": "5b818ec8-0181-4176-91c6-3f31b3c8602a", "ty